note top of run_saber_eval_async
Current SABER MCP Architecture
- inspect_ai native MCP integration via mcp_server_http()
- No custom MCP client implementation needed
- Header-based session/episode context
- Episode-specific tool execution
- Fail-fast configuration validation
- Multi-agent support via AgentAssignment
end note



note bottom of mcp_http
Inspect AI Native MCP Integration
- Uses mcp_server_http() function
- Automatic tool discovery from server
- Session context via HTTP headers
- No custom MCP client management
- Standard MCP protocol compliance
- Seamless agent integration
end note

note right of SessionMCPAPI
Server-Side MCP Implementation
- FastMCP framework
- Header-based context extraction
- Dynamic tool registration per episode
- Episode-specific executor access
- Concurrent execution limits per episode
- Fail-fast parameter validation
end note

note left of RequestHeaders
MCP Context Headers
- X-SABER-Session-ID: session identifier
- X-SABER-Episode-ID: episode identifier
- X-SABER-Orchestration-Env: environment type
- Required for all MCP tool calls
- Validated on each request
end note

